                <pb facs="0882" n="870" sameAs="frus:frus1940v05/pg870"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">622.116/119a: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of
                            State to the Minister in Ecuador</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Long</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1940-08-12T18:00:00-04:00">August 12, 1940—6
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>110. The Department has been informed that the Ecuadoran Consul in New York has
                    been instructed to require exporters to present, beginning today, Ecuadoran
                    import licenses as a requisite for certification of documents.</p>
                <p>Please investigate and report by telegraph.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Welles</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
